WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.745
A trustworthy model should know when it is
operating far from what it has seen.

00:00:04.825 --> 00:00:06.577
Deep neural networks, however,

00:00:06.657 --> 00:00:12.623
often make confident predictions even on inputs
that are wildly different from their training data.

00:00:12.703 --> 00:00:19.585
Classical probabilistic models such as Gaussian
Processes have a built-in sense of distance from the training set,

00:00:19.665 --> 00:00:22.516
but standard deep networks do not, and reliable,

00:00:22.596 --> 00:00:27.280
efficient uncertainty estimation for real
deployments remains an open problem.
